yesterday was supposed to be a  celebratory day and then we got tragic  news about Kobe Bryant and everything  changed in a second  that's Ellen DeGeneres holding back  tears while paying tribute to NBA legend  Kobe Bryant life is short and it's  fragile and we don't know how many  birthdays we have so just we don't want  to have a birthday to celebrate just  celebrate life Kobe and his 13 year old  daughter Gianna were among nine people  killed in a helicopter accident on  Sunday if you haven't told someone you  love them do it now do it tell people  you love them but Ellen wasn't the only  talk-show host to honor the late great  Los Angeles Lakers player Kobe was such  a life force so strong and creative and  inspired that in my head I thought that  he was gonna live forever Jimmy Fallon  opened his show on Monday recalling how  he first met Kobe at a party when they  were both young and relatively unknown I  met Kobe when he was 17 and I was 21 he  was a rookie on the Lakers and I was  just starting out in the comedy scene in  LA we were at a party and we didn't know  anyone at the party Jimmy got emotional  saying they were friends ever since when  we'd run into each other over the years  we'd laugh about that night that we  first met  for all the good things that happen  since and we laugh about how much fun it  was great kids all the stupid mistake  she's made trying to figure out how to  be good dads and the Tonight Show host  explained how we can all honor Kobe's  legacy I think I knew Kobe enough to  know that he rose to any challenge by  digging deeper and getting back to work  so let's honor Kobe gianna and the other  lives that were lost yesterday by  following his example love your family  love your teammates and outwork everyone  else in the gym Jimmy Kimmel opted out  of having a live studio audience on  Monday going forward with a comedy show  didn't feel right considering what  happened yesterday so I'd like to just  speak to you directly and dedicated his  entire show to Kobe he was a bright  light and that's how I want to remember  him he was on the show 15 times we had  many fun and interesting conversations  and tonight we are going to share some  of those to remember him Conan O'Brien  also played back some of his favorite  moments with Kobe over the years and  said this about the type of guest he was  whenever he was on our show he was a joy  to talk with and he always had the  audience in the palm of his hand that's  the guy that I've been thinking about  these past 24 hours and it's that memory  that I would like to share with you  tonight James Corden reflected on the  last time Kobe stopped by his show  following his 2016 retirement from the  NBA he couldn't stop talking about how  excited he was to have all this free  time to devote to his family and to  coach his daughters and I remember  loving hearing him talk like that a man  who had achieved so much in his life was  just so he was so excited just to get to  be a dad for a while  ESPN's Elle Duncan echoed James's  sentiment on SportsCenter praising Kobe  for being a proud dad his third daughter  Bianca was about a year and a half old  at the time so I asked if he wanted more  children and he said that his wife  Vanessa really wanted to try again for a  boy but was sort of jokingly concerned  that it would be on  girl and I was like four girls are you  joking like what would you think how  would you feel and without hesitation he  said I would have five more girls if I  could I'm a girl dad Elle who met Kobe  when she was eight months pregnant with  a daughter of her own broke down in  tears I suppose that the only small  source of comfort for me is knowing that  he died doing what he loved the most a  big dad being a girl dad ET will  continue to be here to bring you all the  latest on this tragic story until next  time I'm Hallie Stevens bye for now
 

